<meta property="og:title" content="Frequently Asked Questions about Managing FACA Committee Records" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Updated: April 2024 1. What records must committee management officers (CMOs) create or maintain? The CMO must keep records that include, but are not limited to: Charter and membership documentation Annual comprehensive review Agency guidelines Closed meeting determinations See 41 CFR 102-3.115 for more specific details. 2. What records should Designated Federal officers (DFOs) or similar agency officers maintain? DFOs should maintain the official records an advisory committee creates or receives." />
